  "solution": {
    "approach": "We need to compute base^exponent for each test case. Using the binary (fast) exponentiation method we repeatedly square the base and multiply it to the result whenever the current exponent bit is 1. This runs in O(log exponent) time and O(1) extra space, which easily satisfies the limits.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(log exponent) per test case, O(T·log exponent) total",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) auxiliary space",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\nimport java.math.BigInteger;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static BigInteger fastPower(BigInteger base, int exponent) {\n        BigInteger result = BigInteger.ONE;\n        while (exponent > 0) {\n            if ((exponent & 1) == 1) {\n                result = result.multiply(base);\n            }\n            base = base.multiply(base);\n            exponent >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringBuilder rawInput = new StringBuilder();\n        String line;\n        while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {\n            rawInput.append(line).append(' ');\n        }\n        String all = rawInput.toString().trim();\n        // Replace escaped newline literals with spaces to handle inputs like \"1\\\\n2 3\"\n        all = all.replace(\"\\\\n\", \" \");\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(all);\n        if (!st.hasMoreTokens()) return;\n        int T = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        StringBuilder output = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < T; i++) {\n            if (!st.hasMoreTokens()) break;\n            BigInteger base = new BigInteger(st.nextToken());\n            int exp = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n            output.append(fastPower(base, exp)).append('\\n');\n        }\n        System.out.print(output.toString());\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
